'' A MEMBER CALL ON A CONSTRUCTOR TEMPORARY -- 'UDT( ).getI( )'. Three of
'' structs/anon-access.bas's verifier failures, and a fourth defect in the same file
'' that the sweep could not see because it counts declines rather than diagnostics.
''
'' EmitTypeCtorInto_ asked for a WRITTEN constructor of the call's arity. With an empty
'' argument list and none written it gave up, having already built the temporary -- so
'' LowerAddr had no receiver to return and the member call was emitted with NONE. The
'' mangled name said member; the call passed no object.
''
'' fbc accepts 'T( )' exactly when T has a constructor at all, measured three ways:
''
''   type Q : a as integer     : b as integer : end type   Q( ) is fbc's error 42
''   type Q : a as integer = 5 : b as integer : end type   Q( ) is accepted
''   type Q : a as integer     : s as string  : end type   Q( ) is accepted
''
'' -- so a field initialiser or a string field is enough, and the synthesised
'' constructor is what the empty spelling runs.
''
'' The second defect is the parser's: 'type<UDT>( ).copyToGlobal( )' at the head of a
'' statement went to the declaration parser, because TYPE starts a declaration, and came
'' back as TKO0406 -- while the identical expression inside a PRINT parsed and lowered.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/ctor-temp-member.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' NO DIAGNOSTIC: the statement-position type literal is the one that reported one.
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 0
'' The temporary is CONSTRUCTED and then passed as the receiver. Both halves matter:
'' the construction is what was missing, and the receiver is what went wrong without it.
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN3UDTC1Ev(@$tmp
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i64 _ZN3UDT4GETIEv(@$tmp
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN3UDT12COPYTOGLOBALEv(@$tmp
'' ...and the written constructor taking arguments, which worked all along.
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i64 _ZN1P4GETVEv(@$tmp
'' GOLDEN: expected/ctor-temp-member.out
